cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use DynaLM in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "DynaLM: run large language models locally on CPU"
type: software
authors:
  - alias: "sajosam"
    website: "https://github.com/sajosam"
repository-code: "https://github.com/dynalm-project/dynalm"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-10-04"
keywords:
  - large language models
  - LLM inference
  - CPU inference
  - GGUF
  - quantization
  - continuous batching
  - OpenAI-compatible API
abstract: >-
  DynaLM is a C++20 inference engine that runs open large language models (Llama, Qwen, Gemma,
  Phi, Mistral, Granite and mixture-of-experts models) on ordinary CPUs. It loads GGUF,
  Hugging Face SafeTensors and GPTQ/AWQ checkpoints, uses hand-written AVX2 and NEON kernels,
  and serves an OpenAI-compatible HTTP API with continuous batching, a paged KV cache,
  chunked prefill and prefix caching.
